  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Total PSA Level (ng/mL)</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Normal Range (&lt;4 ng/mL)</div></td><td><div>Generally indicates a healthy prostate. Elevated levels may still be present in some prostate conditions.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Elevated (4-10 ng/mL)</div></td><td><div>Mildly increased levels may be due to benign prostate conditions or early stages of prostate cancer. Additional tests may be recommended.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Moderately Elevated (10-20 ng/mL)</div></td><td><div>Increased risk of prostate issues, including benign enlargement or cancer. Further evaluation, such as imaging or biopsy, is needed.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>High (&gt;20 ng/mL)</div></td><td class=\"se-table-selected-cell\"><div>Higher levels raise concern for advanced prostate conditions, including cancer. More comprehensive testing and consultation with a specialist are required.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
